IS  - 2050-3121 (Linking)
VI  - 9
DP  - 2021
TI  - Can we improve teaching and learning of percutaneous dilatational tracheostomy's 
      bronchoscopic guidance?
PG  - 20503121211002321
LID - 10.1177/20503121211002321 [doi]
LID - 20503121211002321
AB  - Percutaneous dilatational tracheostomy has become the technique of choice in 
      multiple intensive care units. Among innovations to improve procedural safety and 
      success, bronchoscopic guidance of percutaneous dilatational tracheostomy has 
      been advocated and successfully implemented by multiple groups. Most published 
      literature focuses on the percutaneous dilatational tracheostomy operator, with 
      scarce descriptions of the bronchoscopic particularities of the procedure. In 
      this article, we provide 10 suggestions to enhance specific procedural aspects of 
      bronchoscopic guidance of percutaneous dilatational tracheostomy, and strategies 
      to optimize its teaching and learning, in order to promote learners' competence 
      acquisition and increase patient safety.
