TI  - Guidelines for Percutaneous Dilatational Tracheostomy (PDT) from the Danish 
      Society of Intensive Care Medicine (DSIT) and the Danish Society of 
      Anesthesiology and Intensive Care Medicine (DASAIM).
PG  - C4358
AB  - Percutaneous dilatational tracheostomy is a common procedure in intensive care. 
      This guideline from the Danish Society of Intensive Care Medicine (DSIT) and the 
      Danish Society of Anesthesiology and Intensive Care Medicine (DASAIM) describes 
      indications and contraindications, timing, complications compared to surgical 
      tracheostomy, anaesthesia and technique, decannulation strategy, as well as 
      training and education.
