OWN - NLM
STAT- Publisher
LR  - 20260723
IS  - 0973-7693 (Electronic)
IS  - 0019-5456 (Linking)
DP  - 2026 Jul 23
TI  - Airway and Endotracheal Tubes: Role of POCUS.
LID - 10.1007/s12098-026-06360-0 [doi]
AB  - Airway ultrasound forms an integral part of the Point-of-care ultrasound (POCUS), 
      providing valuable real-time information that supports airway evaluation and 
      management in critically ill patients. POCUS of the airway helps in the airway 
      assessment for difficult laryngoscopy and intubation, confirmation of 
      endotracheal tube (ETT) position, determination of ETT size especially in 
      paediatric patients, identification of the cricothyroid membrane for 
      cricothyrotomy, prediction of postextubation stridor and guidance during 
      percutaneous dilatational tracheostomy. Despite its undeniable utility, airway 
      POCUS has a considerable learning curve and requires structured training and 
      practice. The integration of airway POCUS protocols into the bedside examination 
      of critically ill patients will help to optimise patient safety and outcomes.
