TI  - Endovascular repair of tracheo-innominate artery fistula.
PG  - 36-9
LID - 10.1016/S1875-4597(09)60019-9 [doi]
AB  - Innominate arterial wall rupture with pseudoaneurysm formation was found during 
      angiography in a 39-year-old woman 2 days after she had undergone percutaneous 
      dilatational tracheostomy. Endovascular stent surgery and balloon angioplasty 
      were performed but these procedures failed to control the massive bleeding 
      resulting from an endoleak. We report the clinical presentations and describe the 
      treatment of a tracheo-innominate artery fistula in our patient. We also reviewed 
      the algorithms of management and the rescue options for treating a 
      tracheo-innominate artery fistula.
