TI  - Mediastinitis after percutaneous dilatational tracheostomy.
PG  - 123-4
AB  - In our experience, PDT after total arch replacement, especially after dissection 
      of neck vessels, should be approached with caution. A long skin incision that 
      allows discharge to drain from the wound and a sufficiently long postoperative 
      tracheostomy period to allow tissue healing in the neck are necessary for 
      prevention of mediastinitis.
