DP  - 2022 Jul 29
TI  - Discovery of a rare aberrant artery overlying trachea during open tracheostomy.
LID - 10.1136/bcr-2022-251123 [doi]
LID - e251123
AB  - Tracheostomy is a common surgical procedure for securing a patent airway. 
      Anatomical variations of major vessels overlying the trachea may pose significant 
      bleeding risk during the procedure. Hence, thorough preoperative assessment of 
      the neck and surgeon's intraoperative vigilance are essential. Open tracheostomy 
      is a safer option than percutaneous dilatational tracheostomy. Extra caution with 
      stoma wound care and change of tracheostomy tube are necessary postoperatively if 
      any major vessel is detected in close proximity with the tracheal stoma.
