DP  - 2003 Apr
TI  - Acute fatal haemorrhage during percutaneous dilatational tracheostomy.
PG  - 517-20
AB  - Percutaneous dilatational tracheostomy (PDT) is associated with a number of 
      life-threatening complications. We present a case of massive and fatal arterial 
      haemorrhage that occurred in the intensive care unit during an elective PDT on an 
      86-year-old woman following earlier evacuation of a traumatic subdural haematoma. 
      An avulsed right subclavian artery was found at post mortem. Previous thyroid 
      surgery and aberrant arterial anatomy contributed to the fatal outcome.
